WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.870
Episode 23: The Record Sleeping in the Cave

2
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:09.362
Having safely breached the Siren Strait, the
companions reached the foothills of Mount Dragonhorn,

3
00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:11.840
a rugged coastal mountain range towering
along the continental mainland.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.353
Jagged black granite cliffs cleaved into
the sky like the spine of an ancient dragon,

5
00:00:14.453 --> 00:00:17.810
and each time violent swells crashed against the stone,
concussive booms echoed through showers of crystalline sea spray.

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.685
Accessible only during low tide, the yawning
mouth of a submerged sea cave lay concealed

7
00:00:20.785 --> 00:00:23.780
beneath dense carpets of black moss and barnacles,
entirely invisible to passing imperial patrols.

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.851
It was the legendary Dragon Grotto—the
secret redoubt where the Arcane Holy Knights

9
00:00:26.951 --> 00:00:29.750
had established their rear headquarters
during the First Crusade two decades ago.

10
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.622
Limping forward on his timber
pegleg, Rondol ran his

11
00:00:32.722 --> 00:00:35.720
fingers along a fractured
crevice at the cavern threshold.

12
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.675
[Rondol] "This is the threshold. Twenty winters ago, Lord Balian
and Sir Aleksandar slipped through imperial cordons to shelter

13
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:41.690
thousands of starving refugees in these vaults. The subtle resonance
of the Holy Knights' warding mana still lingers amidst the rock."

14
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:47.660
Bracing his unadorned iron shield,
Kadan took the lead into the gloom.

15
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.630
The interior was remarkably cool and
tranquil, shielded from the coastal tempest.

16
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.487
Phosphorescent lichen clinging
to the stalactites overhead cast

17
00:00:56.587 --> 00:00:59.600
soothing azure luminescence, illuminating
an ancient flagstone passage.

18
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.263
[Celia] Kindling a gentle wind
lantern at the head of her Jade Staff,

19
00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.570
Cilia examined the
subterranean architecture.

20
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:11.540
"Ancient wind wards etched into
the stone walls are still active.

21
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.680
[Ignis] They function as a screening matrix,

22
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.510
neutralizing imperial tracking cantrips."

23
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.421
Touching a weathered
emblem of the White Flame

24
00:01:20.521 --> 00:01:23.480
Order carved into the stone,
Ignis swallowed hard.

25
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:29.450
[Celia] "Somewhere in this vault... lie
the personal records penned by my father."

26
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.532
Entering the great central rotunda,
a colossal round stone table

27
00:01:32.632 --> 00:01:35.420
encircled by twelve high-backed
chairs greeted the companions.

28
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.360
Though fine dust coated the granite, an
ornate iron lockbox resting upon the

29
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.390
table remained pristine and unblemished,
preserved by an ancient kinetic barrier.

30
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.425
Stepping forward, Kadan carefully disengaged the arcane
locking mechanism. Within lay thick vellum campaign journals

31
00:01:44.525 --> 00:01:47.360
bound in cured leather, accompanied by classified tactical
diagrams of the imperial palace's subterranean aqueducts.

32
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:53.330
With trembling fingers, Kadan
opened the first volume.

33
00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.923
Written across the yellowed
parchment in bold,

34
00:01:56.023 --> 00:01:59.300
commanding strokes was the familiar
hand of Master Aleksandar.

35
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:05.270
'First Crusade Expedition Log.

36
00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:11.240
Chronicler: Aleksandar.

37
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.140
[Kadan] May the Light grant that the
blades and shields in our hands never

38
00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.210
become instruments of tyranny, but remain
a steadfast bulwark for the vulnerable.

39
00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.054
[Celia] High Minister Lucian has surrendered

40
00:02:20.154 --> 00:02:23.180
his soul to the shadows of
the Nine Shadows Codex.

41
00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.167
My sworn brother Balian and I
bury the untainted truth within

42
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:29.150
this cavern to preserve the final
hearthfire of the continent.'

43
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:35.120
Tears welled in Kadan's eyes
as he read his master's words.

44
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:41.090
[Ignis] "Master Aleksandar foresaw
everything from the very beginning.

45
00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.228
He knew that even if they were branded
traitors and driven to their graves,

46
00:02:44.328 --> 00:02:47.060
they had to preserve the beacon of
truth for the generations to come."

47
00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:53.030
Cilia placed a comforting
hand upon his shoulder.

48
00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.791
[Ignis] "His noble spirit has survived
inside these cold stone walls,

49
00:02:56.891 --> 00:02:59.000
guiding our steps to this very threshold."

50
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.740
[Ignis] Meanwhile, Ignis lifted a slender

51
00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.970
leather ledger resting at
the bottom of the chest.

52
00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:10.940
It was a secret operational diary
kept by his father, Paladin Balian.

53
00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.620
[Ignis] Detailed within were the security
rotation schedules of the capital,

54
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.910
the subterranean waterways
beneath the cathedral.

55
00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.992
And the layout of Lucian's
subterranean 'Alchemy Dungeons' where

56
00:03:20.092 --> 00:03:22.880
innocent citizens were subjected
to forbidden mana extraction.

57
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.129
[Kadan] Horror and fury
twisted Ignis's features.

58
00:03:25.229 --> 00:03:28.850
"A massive subterranean dungeon was hidden
directly beneath the capital cathedral...

59
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.843
Lucian imprisoned dissenting nobles
and scholars there, injecting them

60
00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:34.820
with Medusa Gorgo's necrotic venom to
synthesize monstrous abominations!

61
00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.663
[Kadan] My father was
condemned to the sulfur mines

62
00:03:37.763 --> 00:03:40.790
because he attempted to demolish
that hellish laboratory!"

63
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.914
[Celia] Ignis slammed his
fist into the stone table,

64
00:03:44.014 --> 00:03:46.760
unheeding of the blood
welling from his knuckles.

65
00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.744
"While my father bled in
chains, I patrolled those gilded

66
00:03:49.844 --> 00:03:52.730
corridors playing the obedient
soldier for his torturers...

67
00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:58.700
How can I ever wash away
such disgraceful blindness!"

68
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:04.670
Kadan gripped Ignis's arm
with unwavering strength.

69
00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:10.640
[Kadan] "Do not torment yourself, Ignis.

70
00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:14.181
Uncle Balian left this blueprint
not so you would weep over the past,

71
00:04:14.281 --> 00:04:16.610
but so your hands could
shatter those iron gates.

72
00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:22.580
[Celia] Now we finish the work they began."

73
00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.530
Suddenly, a mournful shriek
echoed from the ceiling

74
00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.550
stalactites as violet vapor
seeped through the cracks.

75
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.466
Twelve necrotic wraiths planted decades ago by Medusa Gorgo
to desecrate the sanctuary awakened, their serpent tails and

76
00:04:31.566 --> 00:04:34.520
skeletal maws snapping with venomous malice. Bracing his iron
shield, Kadan channeled star-breathing into an impenetrable bulwark.

77
00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.555
[Ignis] "Vile apparitions shall never defile
this sacred haven!" A brilliant sheet

78
00:04:37.655 --> 00:04:40.490
of celestial starlight erupted from Kadan's
shield, blowing back the toxic miasma.

79
00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.665
Vaulting forward, Ignis channeled his
immaculate white flame along his weapon,

80
00:04:43.765 --> 00:04:46.460
incinerating the necrotic cores of
the apparitions in rapid succession.

81
00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.402
[Celia] "Begone, remnants of the shadow!" Sweeping her Jade Staff, Cilia
conjured vacuum blades that cleanly severed the remaining specters.

82
00:04:49.502 --> 00:04:52.430
Confronted by the unified wrath of the three youths, the shadows dissolved
into white ash within minutes, returning serene tranquility to the cavern.

83
00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.828
[Kadan] As they cleared the dais, Cilia discovered a
delicate jade key nestled in the lining of the chest,

84
00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.400
engraved with the intertwined emblems of
the Holy Order and Whispering Wind Island.

85
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.520
[Ignis] "This is the key to the Sealed
Arsenal deeper within the grotto,

86
00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.370
where ancestral relics forged for
the final campaign are enshrined."

87
00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:10.340
Adjusting his silver dagger,
Kadan nodded with grim focus.

88
00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:16.310
[Celia] "To shatter Lucian's legions,
we must elevate our strength.

89
00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.254
[Kadan] Let us claim our forebears' legacy."
United in purpose, the companions took up the jade

90
00:05:19.354 --> 00:05:22.280
key and marched toward the massive adamantine gates
sealed within the deepest recess of the mountain.

91
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.250
